    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d849">

                <pb facs="0935" n="923" xml:id="pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6287: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Beirut</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Palmer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-31T15:00:00-05:00">October 31, 1940—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. The Chargé d’Affaires at Vichy in reporting on French reaction to the Italian
                    attack on Greece<anchor n="37" xml:id="d849-f1"/> states: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“It is privately admitted in certain official circles that if Turkey is
                            drawn in, the allegiance of Syria to the Vichy regime will promptly be
                            severed.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Please comment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
